{"additions":425,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nTab order (the *slot* shown in the header as `n:Label`) was fixed by the registration order in `src/main.rs`. This adds a top-level `pages` node that lists the enabled pages in slot order; a user config can reorder pages or disable the ones it leaves out, while `app { }` bindings keep addressing pages by name.\n\nCloses #114\n\n## Changes\n\n- `assets/default.kdl`: `pages \"git\" \"github\" \"files\" \"docker\" \"procs\" \"actions\" \"worktrees\"` defines the builtin slots.\n- `merge.rs`: `pages` is a replace-wholesale top-level node (like `theme` / `icons`); added to the unknown-block error text.\n- `loader.rs`: `Config::pages()` validates against the builtin `page` blocks (unknown name, duplicate, empty list, non-string args are errors) and falls back to the builtin order when absent; `builtin_page_names()`. `with_user` validates `pages` and every user `page:<name>` binding — a binding to a page that is not listed (or unknown) fails fast with the config path. `app_entries()` drops *builtin* bindings to disabled pages, so `pages \"git\" \"files\" \"worktrees\"` works without unbinding `2`, `4`, `5`, `6` by hand.\n- `src/pages.rs` (new): `build_pages(cfg, cwd, picker)` constructs pages by name in `pages` order and discovers the workdir once; used by `run_tui` and by the `App` tests, so the two cannot drift. `main.rs` only probes the image picker when the Files page is enabled.\n- Header (`page_labels`) and help \"Switch view\" row (`page_keys`) follow the pages vector, so reordering shows e.g. `1:Files 2:Git` with keys `3 / 1`.\n- Docs: `docs/config.md` (merge rule, schema, `### pages` section, example), README / README.ja one sentence + example, CLAUDE.md \"How to add a page\" checklist and architecture line.\n\n### Tests\n\n- `loader.rs`: builtin order matches the `page` blocks; user reorder / disable (builtin keys of disabled pages dropped, remaining keys resolve by name); unknown / duplicate / empty / non-string `pages` errors mention the file; user binding to a disabled or unknown page errors and names the page.\n- `app.rs`: builtin labels order; `pages \"files\" \"git\"` → labels `Files, Git`, keys `3 / 1`; `pages \"worktrees\" \"git\"` → help row `7 / 1` and `1` still switches to Git; `pages \"git\" \"files\" \"worktrees\"` → three pages, `2` does nothing.\n- `merge.rs`: `pages` replaced wholesale.\n\n`cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy --all-targets` (no warnings), `cargo test` (231 passed); `vig config dump` and `--config` with valid / invalid `pages` files checked manually.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- No demo GIF re-recorded (no tape flow changes; header appearance with the builtin config is unchanged).\n- The TUI was not run interactively with a reordered `pages` config (covered by the `App` tests only).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":10,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-30T07:45:47Z","deletions":65,"headRefName":"feat/page-slots","labels":[],"number":117,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLZ1zdw","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\n`build_pages` unconditionally calls `Repo::discover`, making configs that disable git-dependent pages still fail outside a git repo, which conflicts with the new ability to disable pages.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nAdds an explicit, user-configurable page slot order via a new top-level `pages` node in the KDL config, decoupling tab/header slot ordering from Rust module registration order while keeping app keybindings addressing pages by name.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Introduces `pages \"<name>\" ...` as a replace-wholesale top-level config node, with validation (unknown/duplicate/empty/non-string) and fast-fail checks for user `page:<name>` bindings.\n- Centralizes page construction in a new `src/pages.rs` registry, and updates `run_tui` + app tests to use it so page ordering/labels/keys can’t drift.\n- Updates defaults and documentation to describe the new `pages` behavior and examples.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/pages.rs | New page registry that constructs enabled pages in `pages` slot order and returns `(pages, workdir)`. |\r\n| src/main.rs | Switches to `pages::build_pages`, and only probes image picker when Files is enabled. |\r\n| src/core/config/merge.rs | Treats `pages` as a replace-wholesale top-level node and updates error messaging/tests. |\r\n| src/core/config/loader.rs | Adds `Config::pages()` + validation of user app bindings to enabled pages; drops built-in bindings to disabled pages. |\r\n| src/core/app.rs | Updates tests to build enabled pages via the shared registry and verifies slot/label/key behavior under reordering/disabling. |\r\n| assets/default.kdl | Adds the builtin `pages \"git\" ...` list that defines default slots. |\r\n| README.md | Documents `pages` as the way to select/reorder/disable tabs, with an example. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Japanese README update mirroring the `pages` explanation/example. |\r\n| docs/config.md | Adds merge/schema docs and a dedicated `### pages` section with examples and rules. |\r\n| CLAUDE.md | Updates architecture + “How to add a page” checklist to include `pages`/registry requirements. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 10/10 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-30T07:49:06Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"eb018feb09dad8c7dd5aefea43bc5e72ec3f4093"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLZ2qhQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-30T07:55:55Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"eb018feb09dad8c7dd5aefea43bc5e72ec3f4093"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:56:01Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33300353339/job/99227211456","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:56:10Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:50:08Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299963799/job/99226120397","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:45:55Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:46:32Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299963891/job/99226120722","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:45:54Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:48:57Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299963799/job/99226120225","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:45:56Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:49:37Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299963799/job/99226120339","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:45:54Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:50:08Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299963799/job/99226585055","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:50:08Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:56:01Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33300353339/job/99227198860","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:56:02Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:46:43Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299963891/job/99226120788","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:45:55Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:46:44Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299963891/job/99226120784","name":"test (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:45:54Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:56:01Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33300353339/job/99227198987","name":"homebrew","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:56:02Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"}],"title":"✨ Config: explicit page slots via a top-level pages node"}
